id: pm-b9g2cs
title: Sentry release gate aborts valid API queries at a fixed 15-second deadline
description: Exact-tag recovery run 33062893310 failed before package acceptance because the Sentry issues query was aborted at the gate's hard-coded 15-second deadline. The same authenticated query completed successfully with HTTP 200 and an empty issue set in 28.0 seconds under a 60-second diagnostic bound. Replace the brittle constant with a bounded configurable request timeout shared by issue-list and enrichment requests and preserve fail-closed behavior.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: quality-gate,release,reliability,sentry
created_at: "2026-08-27T10:46:02.012Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-27T11:34:04.071Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Default Sentry API request deadline safely covers observed valid latency while remaining bounded; A validated CLI option configures the deadline for deterministic tests and operators; Issue-list and latest-event enrichment use the same deadline contract; Negative-control coverage proves timeout failure remains fail-closed; Live authenticated Sentry query and exact-tag recovery complete without npm republish
parent: pm-ygli86
repro_steps: Run the release Sentry gate with the configured token; observe sentry_query_error timeout at 15 seconds while the identical query succeeds in about 28 seconds with a 60-second bound.
expected_result: The gate allows current valid Sentry latency within a bounded configurable deadline and still fails closed when the deadline is exceeded.
actual_result: A valid Sentry query is aborted after 15 seconds and blocks immutable release recovery.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
