comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T10:46:02.012Z","harness:codex",Duplicate search covered all statuses for Sentry reliability threshold timeout retry and release Sentry API timeout; no item owns the fixed 15-second API deadline defect. pm-ygli86 remains the canonical parent and pm-k6t4yb owns the gate contract.
  "2026-08-27T11:21:24.979Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: exact-tag recovery run 33062893310 failed at the reliability gate because the fixed 15-second AbortSignal deadline expired before Sentry answered. A direct authenticated request needed about 28 seconds. TDD captured four red assertions against the hardcoded 15000ms behavior, then the focused linked suite passed 79/79 after the request-timeout contract was implemented for both issue listing and latest-event enrichment. The first live 60000ms probe subsequently timed out, disproving that production bound; the explicit 120000ms probe passed with checked=true, access_ok=true, zero critical/high issues, and request_timeout_ms=120000. Full local coverage passed 585 files and 8045 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; lint, typecheck, duplication, static assurance, graph assurance, docs links, secret scanning, and pnpm audit all passed."
  "2026-08-27T11:34:03.044Z","harness:codex","Review-loop evidence: CodeRabbit identified that per-request API bounds could accumulate across up to 20 sequential enrichment batches and that Sentry CLI fallback commands omitted the configured timeout. The implementation now gives API and CLI enrichment one shared request-timeout budget, leaves un-enriched rows blocking when that budget is exhausted, and passes the bound to CLI issue-list and event commands. Focused regression coverage passes 80/80, including deterministic budget exhaustion and CLI timeout propagation; eslint, typecheck, and diff checks pass."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T11:21:25.480Z","harness:codex","Provider latency must be validated against the live fail-closed path: a bound that passes once can still be too narrow under transient Sentry latency. Keep the timeout explicit in the workflow, bounded in the CLI contract, recorded in receipts, and shared across list/enrichment requests."
